        "Floating mode: the nearest awcAccordionViewport() or the window stands in for the CSS viewport. CSS position: fixed stacks against the whole document: the panel's z-index lifts the AWC hosts above it, so it paints over later containers of the same AWC tree; an application container between AWC views joins with awcStackingLift(), and an ancestor that clips still clips the panel.",
